 =2({\\pi }^{2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535618 true] [17592186167228 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535618 true] [17592186167228 1100 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535618 true] [17592186167228 1100 "$f(x)∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}\\cos (nx)$\nLet $F(x) =-\\sin (\\frac{x}{3})$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π).]$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for $a_{0}$.$a_{0} =$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535618 false] [17592186167228 1145 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{3}{2}-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357733 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357734 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357735 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357736 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357737 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1041 "selection" 13194139535618 true] [17592186357732 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357735 13194139535618 t